{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01F35ai8pTGAL34VUaQX88sS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty that has grown a substantial R&D control surface bolted onto it. Grounded from the project docs:\n\n- **Core purpose â€” a single-folder GTD-style task/project manager.** Everything lives in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` with plain-markdown files as the source of truth (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files under `domains/`, plus `CANCELLED.md`/`SAVED_FOR_LATER.md` archives). Tasks move through a lifecycle (active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved â†’ restored).\n\n- **What it ships as the running app â€” `anchor_gui.py`** (the one declared deliverable): a self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server that generates the full dashboard HTML on every request and writes changes back to the markdown directly. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` on `http://localhost:8777`. A CLI engine (`anchor.py`) mirrors the same logic and also emits a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **It does task ops + a daily self-test.** API/CLI for done/add/capture/edit/cancel/save/restore, per-domain and completed/cancelled/saved views. A 5 AM scheduled health check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) parses every file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint, and writes a dated report â€” flagging failures with a red dashboard banner.\n\n- **Its major built-out feature is an \"R&D control surface\" for trio-driven development** (the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill trio). It turns each project into a cockpit that launches/manages research, planning, and build sessions as durable, server-side terminal jobs, with cached session/project summaries, grass-catcher idea boards, and pinned deliverables. This has shipped through four iterations, all merged to master:\n  - **v2** â€” session model, validated cached summaries, grass lane, deliverable pinning, an interactive stream-json REPL terminal.\n  - **v3 \"Mission Control\"** â€” real ConPTY terminals (the lone native dep `pywinpty`), per-session git-worktree isolation, a stacking window manager, in-place summaries, stage handoffs, runnable deliverable previews (port-guarded â‰  8777), Ghost World Labs branding.\n  - **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (current, merged `38fd70e`, 2026-06-13) â€” one ConPTY terminal substrate that auto-loads the lane's skill once and greets once (killing the repeating-prompt bug), a claudeâ†”gemini engine toggle, Paradigm-2 inline expanding lane tiles with status lights, per-lane doc roles, a cost/tokens/time project rollup, grass-promote-to-lane, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **Design discipline it holds to:** Python stdlib only (sole exception: lazy `pywinpty` for terminals, enforced by `distro.py`'s import scan), no database/binary formats, markdown as the single source of truth, and every file kept plain-text accessible from any CLI/editor.\n\nNet: it started as a markdown task dashboard and is now also a mission-control console for orchestrating AI research/planning/build sessions, shipped as the single `anchor_gui.py` web app running under a local Windows service."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f06a98d3-ef42-4687-a083-cc4e990f5fec","uuid":"a6225bf2-e943-4eb4-a4a5-2ad53e430387","request_id":"req_011Cc1hcmAvYFLnSCdQzjPXA"}
